fs/fscache/read_helper.c:305:3-6: WARNING: Use BUG_ON instead of if conditi=
on followed by BUG.
Please make sure the condition has no side effects (see conditional BUG_ON =
definition in include/asm-generic/bug.h)

 Use BUG_ON instead of a if condition followed by BUG.

Semantic patch information:
 This makes an effort to find cases where BUG() follows an if
 condition on an expression and replaces the if condition and BUG()
 with a BUG_ON having the conditional expression of the if statement
 as argument.

Generated by: scripts/coccinelle/misc/bugon.cocci

Fixes: 3b7f2f65e5fa ("fscache: read-helper: Provide readahead and readpage =
netfs helpers")
Signed-off-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
---

tree:   https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/dhowells/linux-fs.g=
it fscache-iter
head:   7591b432837ec8742983d3873c89250b204bfba4
commit: 3b7f2f65e5faeb0f3250790d41047e8f81390095 [30/60] fscache: read-help=
er: Provide readahead and readpage netfs helpers
:::::: branch date: 10 hours ago
:::::: commit date: 11 hours ago

Please take the patch only if it's a positive warning. Thanks!

 read_helper.c |    3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/fs/fscache/read_helper.c
+++ b/fs/fscache/read_helper.c
@@ -301,8 +301,7 @@ static void fscache_rreq_terminated(stru
 	if (test_bit(FSCACHE_RREQ_INCOMPLETE_IO, &rreq->flags) &&
 	    in_softirq()) {
 		BUG_ON(work_pending(&rreq->work));
-		if (!queue_work(system_unbound_wq, &rreq->work))
-			BUG();
+		BUG_ON(!queue_work(system_unbound_wq, &rreq->work));
 	} else {
 		fscache_rreq_assess(rreq);
 	}
